  "doc_drift": {
    "_comment": "What a shipped document may not say (docs/guides/doc-style.md, CONVENTIONS section 15). A shipped document is any Markdown file, or its .md.jinja twin, whose path starts with none of history_paths; history_paths are the prefixes whose Markdown is history (a changelog, decisions, plans) and may name a campaign, a slice or a moment. forbidden_phrases maps a regular expression to the reason it is refused: a phrase true of one machine or one person, never a literal host, port or path. tests/integration/test_doc_drift.py reads both: in a shipped document's prose (code spans and fences are illustrations) it refuses a concrete work id in the work_naming grammar, any forbidden phrase, a loopback port that no non-Markdown file declares, and a citation of a document copier.yml never ships. The other keys name the documents a newcomer reads and what each must say, and the same test holds them: one_hop maps an entry document to the documents it links to directly; layout_heading is the README section whose tree lists every top-level directory that ships; roster is the guide index, whose rows each name their audiences from audiences, in that order; limits_guide names every waiver the checkers, the child-process allowlist, the isolation guard and this test grant, and holds the exit-code table scripts/exit_code_table.py generates from scripts/exit_codes.py and from every script make gate_target runs (make check-exit-codes fails a stale one); upgrade_guide gives every copier task and migration its own row in copier's order, names every exclusion and states the copier version floor (template only). settings_reference is the settings reference: tests/integration/test_reference_drift.py holds its rows derived-equal to every key of the JSON files it names, every copier question, make variable, environment variable and command-line flag, with each literal default. features_reference is the feature catalogue: the same test holds its rows to every feature the tree declares (each check letter, annotated make target with its effect label, checker script, copier job, gate test, scripts module another module outside tests/ imports, agent, MCP server, model and runtime adapter, workflow and agent skill) and requires each row to state its limits. A missing or malformed block fails that test.",
