  "make_targets": {
    "_comment": "Every annotated make target opens its `## ` help with an effect label from the closed vocabulary [local] [tree] [read] [cost] [write] (docs/adr/keel/K-0011-make-target-effect-labels.md). scripts/check_structure.py check_W validates this block and the labels; scripts/run_make_target.py runs only a target whose label falls inside gate_effects, sets gate_runner_var=1 last so WRITE_GUARD refuses a [write] target, accepts only the gate_vars as NAME=VALUE variables (each value one path-like word), and fails a run that changed what git sees. unattended_vars are the variables WRITE_GUARD refuses under; write_shapes are target-name suffixes that must be [write]; write_shape_exempt maps a write-shaped target that is not a write to the reason it keeps its label, and an entry naming a target no makefile defines, no write shape matches, no label annotates or that is already [write] is stale (docs/adr/keel/K-0015-write-shape-exemptions-and-guarded-recipe-converse.md); area_dir is the directory of <area>.mk makefiles (null: areas off); effect_proof_skip keeps a [local] target out of tests/integration/test_make_target_effects.py, by name and reason only; effect_proof_kept_dirs names the environment variables (keel ships the XDG base dirs) that sweep keeps while it runs each target under a fresh empty HOME, valued with the directory's relative path strictly inside HOME, used when the caller leaves the variable unset; the sweep fails a target that writes that HOME and does not see writes under the kept dirs; empty_test_selections names a pytest marker a `-m <marker>` recipe may run zero tests of, with the reason as the value (tests/selection_guard.py fails any other run of zero tests, and a run of that marker that ran a test makes the entry stale).",
