  "launcher": {
    "_comment": "Where a long script runs; read by scripts/launch.py, which decides, and scripts/long_scripts.py, which proposes long_scripts entries (docs/adr/keel/K-0020-shared-compute-launcher.md). own_hosts_file is a git-ignored JSON file of fnmatch patterns for the hosts that are one person's own (config/own-hosts.example.json is its shipped twin); absent, unreadable or matching nothing means the host is shared. durations_file is the git-ignored record of each script's last run, keyed by the launch key. A script is long when long_scripts lists it, when its last recorded run took more than long_after_seconds, or when nothing is recorded; long_scripts and default_size give the farm size (cpus, mem_gb, minutes). local_only maps a launch key to the reason it never goes to the farm. credentials maps a launch key to {model_adapter, names}: the only credential names its process may receive. limited.niceness is what running here limited means (os.nice, nothing else). spare.max_load_per_cpu: after the farm did not allocate, this host runs it only when max(load1, load5) / cpus is at most this. farm.adapter names the farm in farm.adapters; the default is none (no farm); an argv adapter submits through its submit argv, with its own bounded wait of wait_seconds, and its reserved not_allocated_status and farm_error_status (1 to 254, not 126, 127 or 130).",
