  "child_env": {
    "_comment": "The environment a process keel's code starts inherits (docs/adr/keel/K-0012-child-process-environment-allowlist.md). scripts/child_env.py build_child_env starts from an empty dict and copies only these names, a name starting with a prefix, make_targets.unattended_vars and gate_vars (so WRITE_GUARD and the interpreter choice survive a hop through a Python doer), and, for a model adapter, its models.credential_env names; scripts/check_structure.py check_X holds every spawn to it. Why each family: PATH, HOME, USER and LOGNAME to find and run tools; LANG, LANGUAGE, TERM, TZ and LC_ for locale and output; the proxy and CA-bundle names because this network intercepts TLS; GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL, GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM so the test suite's hermetic git reaches git, and GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES, because these four choose configuration and the discovery ceiling, not a repository; TEMP, TMP and TMPDIR for scratch; VIRTUAL_ENV and XDG_* for tool caches; SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH for reproducible output; KEEL_REQUIRED_EXTRAS because tests/optional_deps.py reads it to turn a declared surface's skip into a failure, and `make verify` runs its goals through scripts/gate_evidence.py with this environment, so without it a caller who declared a surface required would get a quieter gate than asked for (it carries surface names, never a credential). KEEL_TEST_SCRATCH because tests/conftest.py moves test scratch to the root it names (config tests.scratch_root), so a nested pytest a test starts keeps the root its caller chose. Deliberately absent: every credential (a model adapter's go in models.credential_env), MAKEFLAGS, MFLAGS, MAKELEVEL, MAKEOVERRIDES and MAKEFILES (a nested make must not inherit the outer make's goals; check_X refuses them here), PYTHONPATH (a caller passes it in extra), and GIT_ as a prefix (it would admit GIT_ASKPASS and GIT_SSH_COMMAND). repo_context_names are the variables git binds to the repository it started a process in: `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` (git 2.43.5) plus GIT_NAMESPACE (gitnamespaces(7)) and GIT_QUARANTINE_PATH (githooks(5), pre-receive). githooks(5) tells a hook that runs git in another repository to clear them, so build_child_env drops them unless a call passes repo_context=True, and child_env_policy (hence check_X) refuses names, prefixes, make_targets vars or a models.credential_env list that admits one. config_injection_names and config_injection_prefixes are the configuration-injection family, the variables through which a parent hands git its -c settings (GIT_CONFIG, GIT_CONFIG_COUNT, GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS and the numbered GIT_CONFIG_KEY_<n> and GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_<n>, which override GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL and reach every hook); they hold no location, so they are not repo context, build_child_env never copies one from the parent, and child_env_policy (hence check_X) refuses names, prefixes, make_targets vars or a models.credential_env list that admits one. credentialed_values maps a variable the allowlist copies to the reason this project's children may receive the credential its value carries (an authenticating proxy's user:password@); build_child_env refuses any other copied value carrying user information (scripts/child_env.py carries_credential: a user part in a URL authority, a whole value user[:password]@host:port, or any user part urllib's proxy parser reads in a *_proxy variable), naming the variable and never the value, and an entry no allowlist source copies is a check_X error. credential_value_patterns maps a label to a regular expression a credential's value matches (an Authorization header, a JWT, an opaque token, a PEM private key); build_child_env and the gate runner search every copied value with each, under the same exemptions, and an error names the variable and the label, never the value or the pattern. login_name_schemes lists the URL schemes whose user part is a login name (ssh://git@host): in one of them a user part counts as a credential only with a password; absent, every user part counts. Empty: no child receives a credential through the allowlist. A credential only one model adapter's child needs belongs in models.credential_env instead. Defence-in-depth, not a sandbox: a same-uid child can still read /proc/$PPID/environ.",
    "config_injection_names": ["GIT_CONFIG", "GIT_CONFIG_COUNT", "GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS"],
    "config_injection_prefixes": ["GIT_CONFIG_KEY_", "GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_"],
    "credential_value_patterns": {
      "authorization-header": "(?i)(?:^|[^a-z0-9-])(?:proxy-)?authorization\\s*:(?:\\s+|\\s*[a-z][a-z0-9-]*\\s+)\\S",
      "http-authorization": "^\\s*(?i:(?:(?:proxy-)?authorization\\s*:\\s*)?(?:basic|bearer|digest|negotiate|token))\\s+(?=\\S*[^a-z\\s])[A-Za-z0-9._~+/-]{12,}=*\\s*$",
      "json-web-token": "(?:^|[^A-Za-z0-9_-])eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]*",
      "opaque-token": "^\\s*(?![\\s_~+=-])(?=(?:[^0-9]*[0-9]){2})(?=(?:[^A-Z]*[A-Z]){2})(?=(?:[^a-z]*[a-z]){2})[A-Za-z0-9_~+=-]{32,}\\s*$",
      "private-key": "-----BEGIN [A-Z0-9 ]*PRIVATE KEY-----"
